  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gambia: Improving Access to Justice in The Gambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) The Judicial Training Institute has the knowledge and tools required to develop professional courses and reference materials in new subject areas and deliver these courses to justice sector actors. 2) Magistrates, judges and prosecutors in three (3) rural divisions have improved knowledge, skills and equipment to adjudicate cases of crimes including those of gender-based violence. 3) Commissioners and prosecutors share information on criminal cases through a unified case tracking system. 4) Key justice sector institutions collaborate on the conduct of awareness-raising campaigns targeting women and vulnerable groups.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Judiciary (High Court, Magistrate Court and Judicial Training Institute) and the Ministry of Justice (Attorney General&#x2019;s Office) and the National Human Rights Commission. Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers, especially vulnerable groups, women and victims of human rights violation, including gender-based violence.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to improve access to justice for the people of The Gambia.</narrative>
  </description>
